That's the extension of a term, in this case a predicate: the set of all things 
that satisfy the predicate, so, in the case of 'klama' a set of quintuples of 
objects, places, places, routes between aforementioned places, and modes of 
transportation, such that the first is going from the second to the third along 
the fourth by means of the fifth. That is also a five-place relation, if you 
want to say that the referent should be a relation.




